1 TITL Karaeng
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Tumapaqrisiq Kallonna''' (son of Batara Gowa and I Rerasi Tunijalloq ri Passukkiq) ruled late 1510 or early 1511
2 CONT
2 CONT 1)	During the course of the sixteenth century Gowa came to dominate most of South Sulawesi. This process began with Karaeng Tumapaqrisiq Kallonna, the first Gowa ruler whose reign the Gowa chronicle describes at length.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2)	Ruling from late 1510 or early 1511 to late 1546, Tumapaqrisiq Kallonna laid the foundation for Gowa’s later domination of Makassar
2 CONT
2 CONT 3)	The expansion of Gowa’s influence begun under Tumapaqrisiq Kallonna – militarily, economically, politically – continued throughout the early modern era.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/handle/20.500.12657/34660/376974.pdf?sequence=1&isAllowed=y
2 CONT
