2 CONT In this Tree, based on book "Sadjarah Raden Kandoeroean Soema di Pradja": 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pangeran Panjunan, son of Ratu Petak, son of Pangeran Pasarean, son of Sunan Gunung Jati.
2 CONT
2 CONT Info from Moggi March 2009 (Azmatkhan Tree): 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pangeran Panjunan / Sayyid Abdurrahman, brother of Syekh Datuk Kahfi, Sayyid Abdurrahim (Pangeran Kejaksan) and Syarifah Ratu Baghdad (married to Sunan Gunung Jati), son of Sayyid Sulaiman Al-Baghdadi. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sayyid Sulaiman Al-Baghdadi, brother of Sayyid Husain, one of his son Sayyid Ali Nurul Alam, one of his son Sayyid Abdullah, father of Syarif Nurullah and Syarif Hidayatullah (Sunan Gunung Jati).
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes on May 20, 2009:
2 CONT
2 CONT His name in Joyce FG: Sunan Gunung Jati, link to his other profile:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.geni.com/people/Sunan-Gunung-Jati/6000000003011242251
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT www.petra.ac.id/eastjava/walisongo/jati.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Syarif Hidayatullah, Muhammad Nuruddin, Sayyid Kamil, Syekh Nurullah, and Faletehan are just some of the names which have been given to Sunan Gunung Jati, the wali who is said to have converted the western third of Java Islam virt
2 CONC ually single-handed and to have founded the independent State of Cirebon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Concerning the birth, life, and death of this member of the Wali Songo, there are several conflicting stories, yet the main thread runs as follows: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Syarif Hidayatullah or Syekh Nurullah was born in Pasei, North Sumatra. According to some people, he was the son of Syekh Maulana Ishak and half-brother of Sunan Giri. Following the Portugese invasion of his homeland in 1521, he t
2 CONC ravelled to Mecca, where he stayed for three years. On his return, he entered the service of Sultan Trenggana of Demak, whose younger sister he married.  
2 CONT
2 CONT During the next few years, as a brilliant military commander, he succeeded in subjugating the north west coast of Java as well as the State of Banten. After successfully blocking an attempt by the Portugese to land at Sunda Kelapa
2 CONC  (Jakarta) in 1527, he settled in the region of Cirebon, where he continued to live and teach until his death in A.D. 1570.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sunan Gunung Jati: His Life Upon His Journey
2 CONT
2 CONT Posted on July 26, 2008 by Nia
2 CONT
2 CONT © 2008 Nia’s Match
2 CONT
2 CONT http://niaimaniah.wordpress.com/2008/07/26/sunan-gunung-jati-his-life-upon-his-journey/
2 CONT
2 CONT An Egyptian sultan named Sultan Maulana Mahmud got married to a princess from Pajajaran in 1447, named Nyi Mas Rarasantang (Hj. Syarifah Mudaim) in Tursina mosque. As a result of their marriage, they had two children, named Syarif
2 CONC  Hidayatullah (born: 1448 AD) and Syarif Nurullah (born: 1450 AD). Both Egyptian-Pajajaran spouses made this following agreement: Their sons would act as persons who would convert all people in Java and their counterparts into Isl
2 CONC am.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the Islamic date 5, in the month of Jumadilawal, year 1466 AD, Syarif Hidayatullah made his way to learn Islam from Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). On his way to learn Islam, Syarif Hidayatullah also met Prophet Solomon a
2 CONC nd Prophet Ilyas. Syarif Hidayatullah understood the languages used by jinn (English: genie), satans, angels, animals, and wind. He also instinctively knew the restorative power of plants and fruits. He was also capable of bringin
2 CONC g the dead efficacious plants to life, and was capable of speaking to the dead. He had the power to chill fire, and was capable of staying dry in water. He was also capable of reaching his place destination in no time, within the 
2 CONC blink of eyes.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the Islamic date, 28th Rajab, year 1466 AD, Syarif Hidayatullah ascended to the 6th heaven and met Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). At this time, he was learning Islam from Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). In this yea
2 CONC r, he received the title ‘Insankamil’ from Prophet Muhammad. After embracing the full knowledge taught by Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), he descended to the 5th heaven, and eventually reached the 1st heaven. He descended to
2 CONC  to the Ajrak court from the 1st heaven by riding on white clouds.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Nispu Sya’ban year 1466 AD, Maulana Insankamil Syarif Hidayatullah came to see his mother, Nyi Mas Rarasantang (Hj. Syarifah Muda’im) in the Egyptian court. His journey from the beginning to the end resulted in satisfaction.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1468 AD, Syarif Hidayatullah (Maulana Insankamil) became an Egyptian sultan, named Sultan Maulana Mahmud. In 1472, He was already in Cirebon and met the village chief, named Abdullah Iman = Cakrabuana = Prabu Siliwangi Pajajara
2 CONC n = Prabu Anom = Sri Mangana to introduce Islam. Sultan Syarif Nurullah acted as his replacement as an Egyptian sultan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Syarif Hidayatullah took Ki Syekh Nur Jati as his guru (teacher) in Cirebon and Sunan Ampel in Ampeldenta. In 1479, he was installed as the Head of Cirebon State with the name ‘Yang Sinuhun Kanjeng Susuhunan Jati Purba Panetep Pen
2 CONC ata Agama Awliya Allah Kutubijaman Kholifatur Rasulullah Solallohu Alaihi Wassalam. Until now, he is known as Sunan Gunung jati from Cirebon.
2 CONT
2 CONT During his journey to China, he was successful in converting high-ranking officials, prominent people, and many people in Tartar and its neighbouring states. In 1481 AD, the Great Princess from China, named Princess Ong Tien met S
2 CONC unan Gunung Jati. The Great King of China, Princess Ong Tien’s father, made an experiment. The experiment is explained as follows: Princess Ong Tien put a brass bowl (Indonesian: bokor kuningan) on her stomach made to look like as
2 CONC  if she had been pregnant. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Great King asked Sunan Gunung Jati to answer his question, whether his daughter was pregnant or had a disease. Sunan Gunung Jati answered that Princess Ong Tien was pregnant. Princess Ong Tien was furious, Sunan Gunung Jati wa
2 CONC s lashed out and chased away. In fact, she WAS pregnant under God’s will without having a sexual intercourse with an opposite sex.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sunan Gunung Jati continued his journey on his Islamic mission from one place to another, until he reached the Cirebon court close to Gunung Sembung.
2 CONT
2 CONT Princess Ong tien and The Great King of China along with 1524 people riding on three ships and the treasures inside sailed to catch Sunan Gunung Jati in Cirebon. Sunan Gunung Jati was in Luragung court. The Great King of China, Pr
2 CONC incess Ong Tien, and their entourage went to Luragung to meet Sunan Gunung Jati. At that time, Sunan Gunung Jati was sitting with his assistant, named Gedeng Kemuning. The Great King of China handed over the pregnant Princess Ong 
2 CONC Tien along with all of his belongings to Sunan Gunung Jati. Sunan Gunung Jati treated The Great King of China and Princess Ong Tien well.
2 CONT
2 CONT The time came for Princess Ong tien to give birth. Her son was named Prince Kuningan (Arya Kemuning). Arya Kemuning lived in Kuningan, Cirebon. The Great King of China and Princess Ong Tien converted to Islam. Princess Ong Tien ma
2 CONC rried to Sunan Gunung Jati, and she received a title, “Nyi Mas Rara Sumanding”.
2 CONT
2 CONT After several years, Princess Ong Tien or Nyi Mas Rara Sumanding died.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sunan Gunung Jati. Merge Terah Bojongjati with book  Sejarah Perintisan Penyebaran Islam di Tatar Sunda. Lahir 1448, wafat 19 september 1568 di Cirebon, makamnya di Astana Gunung Jati (Cirebon). Raja Pakungwati (Cirebon), 1479-156
2 CONC 8. Susuhunan Cirebon. Ingkang Sinuhun Kanjeng Susuhunan Jati Purba Panetep Panatagama Awliya Allah Kutubid Jaman Khalifatur Rasulullah s.a.w. Pandita Ratu, Pate Cherimon, Pati Cirebon, Adipati Cirebon.
2 CONT ==============================================================================
