1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A. '''Tumamenang ri Gaukanna (Sultan Ala’uddin)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Tunipasuluq was the sibling of Tumamenang ri Gaukanna'''. After his elder sibling was expelled he was installed as ruler by his mother. Entering his seventh year, [26r] he became ruler. His personal name, may I not be cursed, w
2 CONC as I Manngarangi. His royal name was I Daeng Manraqbia. His Arabic name was '''Sultan Alau’ddin'''. For twelve years he ruled then entered Islam. A Minangkabau converted him. Kota Tanga was the name of his homeland. Katte Tunggala
2 CONC q was his personal name. He settled on land at the end of Pammatoang. Named I Datoq ri Bandang, he led the karaeng into Islam on the ninth night of Jumadilawal, on Friday in 1014 of the Islamic calendar, 22 September 1605 of the C
2 CONC hristian calendar.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/handle/20.500.12657/34660/376974.pdf?sequence=1&isAllowed=y
2 CONT
2 CONT B. '''Tumamenang ri Gaukanna (Sultan Ala’uddin)''' '''Tunipasuluq was the sibling of Tumamenang ri Gaukanna'''. After his elder sibling was expelled he was installed as ruler by his mother. Entering his seventh year, [26r] he beca
2 CONC me ruler. His personal name, may I not be cursed, was I Manngarangi. His royal name was I Daeng Manraqbia. His Arabic name was '''Sultan Alau’ddin'''. For twelve years he ruled then entered Islam. A Minangkabau converted him. Kota
2 CONC  Tanga was the name of his homeland. Katte Tunggalaq was his personal name. He settled on land at the end of Pammatoang. Named I Datoq ri Bandang, he led the karaeng into Islam on the ninth night of Jumadilawal, on Friday in 1014 
2 CONC of the Islamic calendar, 22 September 1605 of the Christian calendar
2 CONT
2 CONT C. '''Tumamenang ri Gaukanna (brother of Tunipasuluq) ruled 1593 to 15 June 1639                                                                               Sultan Alau’ddin lived 1586 to 15 June 1639'''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT i.	The conversion of the kingdom to Islam is dated as '''September 22, 1605 when the 14th king of Tallo-Gowa''' kingdom, '''Karaeng Matowaya Tumamenaga Ri Agamanna''', converted to Islam, where later changed his name to '''Sultan 
2 CONC Alauddin'''. He ruled the kingdom from 1591 to 1629.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sultanate_of_Gowa
2 CONT
2 CONT ii.	Quite probably individual Makassarese converted before 1605, but on '''22 September of that year Karaeng Matoaya''' formally and publicly embraced Islam, followed soon thereafter by '''Sultan Ala’uddin''' (the Islamic title by
2 CONC  which this first Muslim ruler of Gowa is known).
2 CONT
2 CONT iii.	 Nevertheless, Karaeng Matoaya and Sultan Ala’uddin fundamentally changed South Sulawesi. Matoaya and Ala’uddin launched campaigns known as ‘Wars of Islamization’ throughout and beyond the peninsula. Between 1608 and 1611 all
2 CONC  the major polities of South Sulawesi south of the highland Toraja were forcibly converted to Islam.  
2 CONT
2 CONT iv.	All recount the reign of Sultan Ala’uddin’s successor Sultan Malikussaid (reign 1639 to 1653), and many contain accounts of his successor, Sultan Hasanuddin (reign 1653 to 1669). Hasanuddin was the last independent ruler of Go
2 CONC wa, and the one who oversaw the debacle of the Makassar Wars (1666-1669), which ended in 2 Andaya 1984; Cummings 2001; Noorduyn 1956; Pelras 1985. 8 A chain of kings Gowa’s subjugation (Andaya 1981). Though the wars are not descri
2 CONC bed in the chronicle, following the conquest he abdicated, and died soon after. With his death the Gowa chronicle ends too, a poignant recognition that a glorious era had come to a close.
2 CONT
2 CONT v.	The conversion of the kingdom to Islam is dated as September 22, 1605 when the 14th king of Tallo-Gowa kingdom, '''Karaeng Matowaya Tumamenaga Ri Agamanna''', converted to Islam, where later changed his name to Sultan Alauddin.
2 CONC  He ruled the kingdom from 1591 to 1629. His conversion to Islam is associated with the arrival of three ulama from Minangkabau: Datuk Ri Bandang, Datuk Ri Tiro and Datuk Ri Pattimang.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://iracing.fandom.com/wiki/Sultanate_of_Gowa 
2 CONT
2 CONT vi.	History. Islamic Sultanate. (Исламский Султанат) Traces of Islam in South Sulawesi existed since the 1320s when the first Sayyid in South Sulawesi, namely Jamaluddin Sayyid al-Akbar al-Husseini, who is a grandfather of Wali So
2 CONC ngo. The transformation of the Kingdom in Islam, 22 September, 1605, when the 14th king of Tallo-Kingdom of Gowa, Karaeng Ri Matowaya Tumamenaga Agamanna convert to Islam, where he changed his name to Sultan Alauddin. He ruled the
2 CONC  Kingdom from 1591 1629. His conversion to Islam is associated with the arrival of three ulama from Minangkabau: Datuk Bandang Ri Tiro, and Dato and Dato Patimang.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://amp.en.google-info.cn/44783747/1/sultanate-of-gowa.html 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/handle/20.500.12657/34660/376974.pdf?sequence=1&isAllowed=y
2 CONT
