1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Sheikh Yusuf al Makassari (1626-1699)=
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Overview ==
2 CONT '''Sheikh Yusuf al Makassari, born Abadin Tadia Tjoessoep''', was an influential Indonesian Muslim scholar, leader, and nobleman of Makassar descent. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was also known as '''Muhammad Yusuf''' and '''Tuanta Salamaka ri Gowa''' ("our savior teacher from Gowa").
2 CONT == Key Details ==
2 CONT * Born: July 3, 1626, in Makassar, Gowa Sultanate (present-day Indonesia)
2 CONT * Died: May 23, 1699, in exile at the Cape of Good Hope, South Africa
2 CONT * Parents: (14th King of Luwu & Prince of Gowa) [https://www.geni.com/people/Sultan-Abdullah-Khaidir/6000000040663601545?through=6000000041944206059 Sultan Abdullah Khaidir], and [https://www.geni.com/people/Sitti-Aminah-I-Tubiani
2 CONC -Daeng-Kunjung/6000000040663584539?through=6000000041944206059 Sitti Aminah (I-Tubiani Daeng Kunjung)]
2 CONT * Renamed in childhood by his uncle [https://www.geni.com/people/Sultan-Alauddin/6000000210739704830 Sultan Alauddin] of Gowa Sultanate
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Royal Lineage==
2 CONT '''Sheikh Yusuf''' came from a distinguished royal lineage, with ancestors ruling various '''Makassar Kingdoms including Gowa, Tallo, and Luwu'''. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His paternal grandmother, '''Empress I-Sambo Daeng Niasseng''', held multiple royal titles and was a key figure in regional politics.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Education and Religious Journey==
2 CONT * 1644-1664: Spent 20 years studying in Arabia, including performing the Hajj to Mecca
2 CONT * Became a prominent Islamic scholar and teacher
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Political and Religious Roles==
2 CONT * c.1660: Marries [https://www.geni.com/people/Karaeng-Kontu/6000000173130592827?through=6000000041944206059 Princess Karaeng  Kontu] the daughter of 14th King of Gowa/Sultan of Gowa, (his 1st cousin) mother of https://www.geni.co
2 CONC m/people/Sitti-Aminah/6000000173133970350?through=6000000041944206059
2 CONT * 1664-1680: Settled in Serang, Banten, Indonesia
2 CONT * 1665: Marries [https://www.geni.com/people/Ratu-Ayu-Siti-Khafifah-Sitti-Hafsah-Karaeng-Pane/6000000040664006834?through=6000000041944206059 Princess Ratu Ayu] the daughter of the 6th Sultan of Banten, mother of https://www.geni.
2 CONC com/people/Ratu-Bagus-Tubagus-Malolowa/6000000024695167116?through=6000000041944206059
2 CONT * 1668: Appointed as a religious advisor to the Sultanate of Gowa
2 CONT * Led resistance against Dutch colonial rule
2 CONT
2 CONT == Exile and Later Life==
2 CONT * 1684: Captured and imprisoned by the Dutch
2 CONT * 1693: Exiled to the Cape of Good Hope, South Africa
2 CONT * 1694-1699: Established the first Muslim community in South Africa
2 CONT
2 CONT == Legacy and Impact==
2 CONT *  Religious scholarship: Became an important Islamic teacher and scholar
2 CONT * Political influence: Served as a religious advisor and led rebellion against Dutch colonial rule
2 CONT * Spread of Islam: Established the first Muslim community in South Africa
2 CONT * Cultural legacy: Honored with a Kramat (Shrine) in Cape Town; Zandvliet renamed Macassar in his honor
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Significance==
2 CONT '''Sheikh Yusuf's life bridged multiple cultures and continents''', illustrating the complex interplay of religion, politics, and colonialism in the 17th century. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His royal lineage, religious scholarship, and political activism combined to make him a pivotal figure in the history of Indonesia and South Africa. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Despite exile, his influence continued through the establishment of Muslim communities in new territories.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
