1 NAME Muzaffar Shah I /ibni al-Marhum Sultan Mahmud Shah/
2 GIVN Muzaffar Shah I
2 _MARNM ibni al-Marhum Sultan Mahmud Shah
2 NICK Marhum Tanah Abang (t28)
1 NAME Sultan Muzaffar Shah I [Sultan Perak Pertama 1528 - 1549]
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Tanah Abang Telok Bakong
2 ADDR
3 CITY Lambor Kanan
3 STAE Perak
3 CTRY Malaysia
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1505
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1549
1 OCCU 1st Perak Sultan (1528 -1549)
1 TITL Sultan
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1st Sultan of Perak: Sultan Muzaffar Shah ibni Almarhum Sultan Mahmud Shah (1528-1549)
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Perak, with its capital at Bruas, was a province of Melaka. When Melaka fell to Portuguese in 1511, Sultan Mahmud fled, eventually becoming Sultan of Kampar-Sumatra which was also a province of Melaka. Perak was left to its own fa
2 CONC te and needed a ruler. A mission, headed by Tun Saban and Nakhoda Kassim, to ask Sultan Mahmud for one of his sons to come and rule over Perak. Sultan Mahmud then instructed his second son from his marriage to Puteri Onang Kening 
2 CONC of Kelantan, Raja Muzaffar, to go forth to Perak. On receiving such good tidings, Tun Saban returned to Perak and prepared 77 elephants bearing gifts to await their new Sultan at the estuary of Sungai Perak.
2 CONT
2 CONT Raja Muzaffar, carried with him the state regalia, comprising the sword Chura Si-Manjakini, a keris, the Cap Kayu Cempa (which bore the inscription ‘Sultan Muhammad Shah Dzil Allah Fil-Alam’), the nobat and the Surat Chiri, to Per
2 CONC ak. During a stop at Klang to meet his relatives, Raja Muzaffar met Nakhoda Tumi of Manjong, a merchant ship captain who sailed regularly to Perak. Nakhoda Tumi came on board Raja Muzaffar’s ship and continued their onward journey
2 CONC  to Perak. On arriving at Beting Beras Basah, the ship got stuck despite various efforts. Raja Muzaffar then called (seru):
2 CONT
2 CONT Sekongkong Tanah Minangkabau Selilit Pulau Perca Di lengkong ular Saktimuna Perpisahan beta di Selat Melaka Jika sah beta Raja berdaulat Lepaslah sekalian malapetaka.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following the seru, the ship somehow was released and was able to continue in its journey. On arrival in Perak, Raja Muzaffar was met and welcomed by Tun Saban and the joyful people of Perak, who shouted “Daulat Tuanku!” thrice. T
2 CONC he people then escorted him to Tanah Abang[1] where he then instructed his people to build his residence. He was duly installed and was styled Sultan Muzaffar Shah, during which the mestika embun was presented to him by Tok Temong
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT After his installation, he appointed Tun Mahmud, son of Tuan Tun Isap Barakah and Puteri Siat of Bruas, to be his Bendahara. After holding this post for some time, Bendahara Mahmud was invited by Sultan Alauddin Riayat Shah II of 
2 CONC Johor (brother to Sultan Muzaffar Shah) to be Bendahara at his court.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sultan Muzaffar asked for the hand of Tun Merah, daughter of Tun Saban, but was refused. One day when Tun Saban was away from his house, having gone upstream on one of his periodical visits, Sultan Muzaffar abducted Tun Merah and 
2 CONC kept her in his palace. This so angered Tun Saban that he declared war on the Sultan. He built a fort at Kuala Temong from where he defied the Sultan’s forces. Secure in the fact that his skin could not be pierced by bullets (keba
2 CONC l), he used to laugh at the efforts made to shoot him down.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sultan Muzaffar then issued a proclamation that whoever could kill Tun Saban would be awarded with the highest chieftaincy in the state. Within the army of the Sultan was  a soldier of fortune named Megat Terawis ibni Almarhum Dau
2 CONC lat Pagar Ruyong, a scion of the great imperial house of Minangkabau. Megat Terawis was ‘born with a silver bullet in each hand’, each bullet bearing the inscription:
2 CONT
2 CONT “Inilah peluru anak Raja Pagar Ruyong – di mana ia jatuh, di situlah tuannya menjadi tuan.“[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Megat Terawis faced Tun Saban, and fired his matchlock (istinggar). The bullet struck Tun Saban on his chest but fell to the ground, as it had not pierced Tun Saban’s skin. Tun Saban picked it up, read the inscription and knew tha
2 CONC t his hour of doom had come. He then sent for Megat Terawis, named him as his heir, expressed regret for his past hostilities to the Sultan and married Megat Terawis to one of his daughters, Tun Bongsu Bangsawan. Tun Saban then su
2 CONC ccumbed to his injury from the mystical bullet and was interred at Changkat Merah in Hulu Perak. Megat Terawis was rewarded with the highest chieftaincy in the state carrying the title Bendahara Paduka Raja[3].
2 CONT
2 CONT Sultan Muzaffar Shah later moved his residence to Kota Lama Kanan near Kuala Kangsar. However, Almarhum mangkat in 1549 and was interred at Tanah Abang. The title Marhum Tanah Abang was conferred on him after death.
2 CONT
