2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Pandita Perabu Darma Suci had Hinduism grow in the 13th century. His name was well known in Pajajaran Kingdom, but also in Central Java, Jayakarta (Jakarta) and even Sumatra. In poetry work of those days, many were written on visi
2 CONC tors who came from other neighboring kings to Talaga. Whether these visits were actually familial visits, it was not really known. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Remnants from this Kingdom included copper and brass work including Gong, Steel Harness used for war. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He passed in the 14th century, leaving two sons, 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Bagawan Garasiang - 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Sunan Talaga Manggung
